class:: VpatternPlayer
summary:: Plays a visual pattern via an EventStreamPlayer
categories:: Libraries>VisualServer
related:: Classes/Vbind, Classes/EventStreamPlayer, Classes/VisualServer, Guides/VisualServer

description::

Manages playback of a visual pattern. Created implicitly by code::Pattern:vplay:: (added to link::Classes/Pattern:: by this library), so you rarely construct it directly.

It calls code::pattern.play(clock, Event.new, quant):: — an strong::empty:: proto event, not code::nil::. Passing code::nil:: would make link::Classes/EventStreamPlayer:: copy code::Event.default:: into every event, leaking SC's audio machinery (code::sustain:: as a Function, code::legato:: 0.8) as own keys and breaking the visual envelope model. link::Classes/Event#-play:: still attaches the default parent for code::~play::/code::~eventTypes::, so scheduling and dispatch keep working.

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
argument:: pattern
The visual pattern (e.g. a link::Classes/Vbind::).
argument:: clock
Default link::Classes/TempoClock#*default::.
argument:: view
Fallback view symbol (default code::\default::).
argument:: server
Default link::Classes/VisualServer#*default::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

method:: play
Build and play the link::Classes/EventStreamPlayer::.
argument:: quant
returns:: this player.

method:: stop
Stop playback and clear the player.

method:: pause
method:: resume
method:: isPlaying
Returns true while the underlying player is playing.

method:: pattern
method:: clock
method:: view
method:: server
method:: player
The underlying link::Classes/EventStreamPlayer:: (read/write).

EXAMPLES::

code::
p = Vbind(\x, Pwhite(-0.8,0.8), \dur, 0.25, \view, \demo).vplay;  // returns a VpatternPlayer
p.isPlaying;
p.pause; p.resume;
p.stop;
::
